From f1c968eae6934b88a091230a2a5c0b65f27ab18a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:51:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Voice delivery tag: review round 1 fixes M1, M2 (endpoint
 and walker), m1 to m5, m7, n1, n3, n5

M1: the endpoint never sends the client's note: TtsLineExtractor#delivery_for
returns the ink's own note for the speaker and line, and that note is keyed,
voiced and recorded. Lookalike (fullwidth, emoji) notes select it but add nothing.
M2: an unmatched note is dropped and the line voiced untagged, never refused.
InkLineWalker now carries a #delivery: note across a plain divert to the
target's first line, as inkjs does; parity test against inkjs on the reviewer's
scratch inks plus a divert fixture.
m1: a tagged line falls back to its untagged or previous-model clip after a
quota error or failed generation. m2: preload sends no note. m3/m4: a note with
nothing left after normalising, or over 200 characters, is no note; Unicode
spaces collapse on both sides. m5: the pruner's expected set reads tagged lines
with the scenario's globals too. m7: one walk for spoken and delivered lines,
endpoint cache keyed by scenario and stamp, bounded LRU of 32.
n1: delivery is a presentation tag for deferred replies. n3: note looked up
after the NPC and text checks. n5: unused isDeliveryTag export dropped.
